Commit:     welpy-cw <h.w.forms@arcor.de>
CommitDate: Tue Mar 17 16:15:05 2026 -0600

    Bug 2017003 - Harden layout sequence and fix accessibility in new mail alert. r=arschmitz


    This hardens the new mail alert's initialization sequence to prevent
    potential race conditions between asynchronous Fluent localization, layout
    calculation, and OS window sizing. It also resolves an accessibility bug
    where screen readers announced fallback strings before JS initialization.

    - Kick off Fluent translation at `DOMContentLoaded` so it runs in parallel
      with window asset loading, and await `document.l10n.translateElements`
      to ensure the DOM is ready before measuring `scrollHeight`.
    - Replace the blind setTimeout with a robust Promise race to position the
      alert. It pre-snaps the window to hide native OS shell flashes, listens
      for the organic `resize` event (filtering out stray layout shifts by
      verifying dimensions), and falls back to a 100ms timer for OS window
      managers that coalesce rendering events.
    - Retain the `resize` listener permanently so it acts as an anchor if the
      OS resizes the window later.
    - Move `role="alert"` from the `body` to `#alertTextBox` and remove
      static `data-l10n` attributes from `#alertTitle`. The container now
      starts empty, ensuring ARIA mutations only trigger screen readers
      once the real data is injected.
    - Add `{ once: true }` to the `dragend` listener to prevent a memory leak
      on the source node.
    - Add `contain: content` to `#alertTextBox` to optimize layout reads.

    Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D284694

